# SPRINT 7: Paribhasha — Valid Program (must compile and execute cleanly)
#
# This program obeys all three Paribhasha constraints:
#   P1: No Anuvrtti as first statement
#   P2: Lopa only after a write to the same target
#   P3: Vrddhi (Ring 0) only on Asiddha targets (>= 0x50)
#
# The compiler accepts this. The firmware executes it. Both proofs together
# demonstrate that Paribhasha rejects exactly what is wrong and permits
# exactly what is right — nothing more, nothing less.

सञ्ज्ञा वाक् = 0x30 ।
सञ्ज्ञा यन्त्र = 0x60 ।

तन्त्रशास्त्रम् {
    # Valid: explicit write to Vak first (P1 satisfied — not Anuvrtti at start)
    वाक् लिखति ।

    # Valid: Anuvrtti after explicit write (P1 satisfied — context exists)
    लिखति ।

    # Valid: Lopa after write to same target (P2 satisfied)
    वाक् लोपः ।

    # Valid: Vrddhi store to Yantra (0x60 >= 0x50, Asiddha) (P3 satisfied)
    यन्त्रै स्थापयति ।
}
